358	<!-- ============================================================ -->
359	<section>
360	<h2>5. Custom Blocks — Creating Instruments Without Writing Python</h2>
361	
362	<p>The custom-block system lets you define a new instrument entirely in a JSON file. Drop it in <code>silmulator/custom_blocks/</code> (or <code>~/.silmulator/custom_blocks/</code> for personal blocks) and it appears in the library on next launch.</p>
363	
364	<h3>The minimal spec — Hello World example (shipped with Silmulator)</h3>
365	<pre><code><span class="cm">// silmulator/custom_blocks/hello_world.json</span>
366	{
367	    <span class="attr">"name"</span>:         <span class="str">"Hello World"</span>,
368	    <span class="attr">"manufacturer"</span>: <span class="str">"Silmulator"</span>,
369	    <span class="attr">"model"</span>:        <span class="str">"HELLO-1"</span>,
370	    <span class="attr">"color"</span>:        <span class="str">"#3a6f3a"</span>,    <span class="cm">// CSS hex — the block header tint</span>
371	    <span class="attr">"ports"</span>: [
372	        {<span class="attr">"id"</span>:<span class="str">"IN"</span>,  <span class="attr">"label"</span>:<span class="str">"IN"</span>,  <span class="attr">"x"</span>:<span class="num">0.0</span>, <span class="attr">"y"</span>:<span class="num">0.5</span>},  <span class="cm">// left-middle</span>
373	        {<span class="attr">"id"</span>:<span class="str">"OUT"</span>, <span class="attr">"label"</span>:<span class="str">"OUT"</span>, <span class="attr">"x"</span>:<span class="num">1.0</span>, <span class="attr">"y"</span>:<span class="num">0.5</span>}   <span class="cm">// right-middle</span>
374	    ],
375	    <span class="attr">"commands"</span>: {
376	        <span class="attr">"HELLO"</span>:  <span class="str">"world"</span>,        <span class="cm">// any matching command → always returns "world"</span>
377	        <span class="attr">"*IDN?"</span>:  <span class="str">"Silmulator,HELLO-1,SIM000001,1.0.0"</span>,
378	        <span class="attr">"ECHO"</span>:   <span class="str">"echo:{0}"</span>     <span class="cm">// {0} substitutes the first SCPI parameter</span>
379	    }
380	}</code></pre>
381	
382	<h3>Three command value types</h3>
383	<table>
384	  <tr><th>Value format</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr>
385	  <tr><td><code>"some string"</code></td><td>Always returned verbatim</td><td><code>"HELLO": "world"</code></td></tr>
386	  <tr><td><code>""</code> (empty)</td><td>Write-only — accepted, no response</td><td><code>"OUTP": ""</code></td></tr>
387	  <tr><td><code>"echo:{0}"</code></td><td>Substitutes SCPI positional params</td><td><code>ECHO 42</code> → <code>"echo:42"</code></td></tr>
388	</table>
389	
390	<h3>How discovery works at startup</h3>
391	<pre><code><span class="cm"># canvas.py:40 — runs at import time</span>
392	<span class="kw">try</span>:
393	    <span class="fn">register_custom_blocks</span>(BLOCK_REGISTRY)
394	<span class="kw">except</span> Exception:
395	    <span class="kw">pass</span>   <span class="cm"># one bad JSON file cannot block app startup</span></code></pre>
396	
397	<p><code>register_custom_blocks()</code> calls <code>discover_specs()</code> which <code>glob("*.json")</code>s both <code>silmulator/custom_blocks/</code> and <code>~/.silmulator/custom_blocks/</code>. Each valid spec is turned into a live Python class by <code>make_custom_block_class(spec)</code> and added to <code>BLOCK_REGISTRY</code> — the same dictionary the built-in blocks live in.</p>
398	
399	<div class="callout">
400	  <div class="callout-label">📌 The full pipeline</div>
401	  <code>hardware_docs/keysight/E36312A/scpi_commands.md</code>
402	  → <em>(you author a spec)</em>
403	  → <code>silmulator/custom_blocks/keysight_e36312a_custom.json</code>
404	  → <em>(app starts)</em>
405	  → <code>discover_specs()</code> → <code>make_custom_block_class()</code>
406	  → appears in Library panel as <strong>"Keysight E36312A Custom"</strong>
407	</div>
408	</section>
