411	<section>
412	<h2>6. Often Confused: Ports vs. Wires vs. Signals</h2>
413	
414	<p>Three things in this project carry the word "connection" — they are completely different layers:</p>
415	
416	<table>
417	  <tr><th>Concept</th><th>Python class</th><th>Where</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
418	  <tr>
419	    <td><strong>Port</strong></td>
420	    <td><code>ConnectionPort</code></td>
421	    <td><code>base_block.py</code></td>
422	    <td>A clickable endpoint on a block. Holds <code>connected_to</code> reference. Visual + structural.</td>
423	  </tr>
424	  <tr>
425	    <td><strong>Wire</strong></td>
426	    <td><code>WireItem</code></td>
427	    <td><code>canvas.py</code></td>
428	    <td>A drawn line between two ports. Lives in the scene. Routes Code Input commands when <code>_get_connected_blocks()</code> is called.</td>
429	  </tr>
430	  <tr>
431	    <td><strong>Qt Signal</strong></td>
432	    <td><code>pyqtSignal</code></td>
433	    <td><code>canvas.py</code></td>
434	    <td>A Python-level event notification (e.g. <code>wire_added</code>). Carries metadata to listeners like the status bar. Not visible on canvas.</td>
435	  </tr>
436	</table>
437	
438	<p><strong>Common confusion:</strong> people think wires route SCPI commands in real-time, like a bus. They don't — a wire's only runtime effect is to be traversed by <code>_get_connected_blocks()</code> when the Code Input block runs its parsed commands. For direct console commands the wire is purely visual.</p>
439	
440	<table>
441	  <tr><th></th><th>Port</th><th>Wire</th><th>Qt Signal</th></tr>
442	  <tr><td>Visible on canvas?</td><td>✓ blue/green circle</td><td>✓ gold line</td><td>✗ invisible</td></tr>
443	  <tr><td>Persisted in layout file?</td><td>✓ (via block)</td><td>✓ src_block/port + dst_block/port</td><td>✗ ephemeral</td></tr>
444	  <tr><td>Routes SCPI commands?</td><td>✗</td><td>Only for Code Input → connected blocks</td><td>✗</td></tr>
445	  <tr><td>One per block?</td><td>✗ (many)</td><td>✗ (many)</td><td>✗ (several types)</td></tr>
446	</table>
447	</section>
