443	- template.format(*["42"]) → "echo:{0}".format("42") → "echo:42"
444	So the block responds with "echo:42".
445	The three branches: (1) empty string → write-only, returns ""; (2) no "{" → always return the template verbatim (e.g. "STATUS?": "OK" always returns "OK"); (3) "{0}", "{1}", etc. → substitute positional SCPI params.`
